# Chat instructions — `<MARKER>`

> Project instructions for chat-Claude (claude.ai). Pair file to repo-side `CLAUDE.md`. Auto-loaded once attached to the Claude.ai project's Project knowledge.

## Project

- **Marker:** `<MARKER>` — repo-scoped. Linear ticket IDs use the team's key prefix; the marker lives in titles (`[<MARKER>] feature-name`) and document IDs (`[<MARKER>-DOC-NNNN]`).
- **Repo:** see Project knowledge for the GitHub URL.
- **Linear workspace:** connected via the Linear connector at project level.

## Connectors required

- **Linear** (project-level). Used to read/write tickets, documents, and cycles.
- **GitHub Integration** (project-level). Syncs the repo into Project knowledge (one-time, and on refresh) so chat-Claude can retrieve repo files — skills, rules, templates, prior specs — via Project-knowledge search. There is no callable GitHub file-read tool in chat; the Integration's job is the *sync*, not live reads. The repo must also be added to *this* Project's knowledge (Project knowledge → **GitHub** → select repo → **Add**).

If either is disconnected, halt and ask the founder to attach it before proceeding. If the GitHub Integration is on but a repo primitive can't be retrieved, the repo is not synced into this Project's knowledge — attach it via the click-path above.

## Communication profile

> Generated from `docs/product/founder-profile.md` (the canonical source, authored at `/onboard` step 3b). Tells chat-Claude how to talk to the founder. Re-render with `/onboard --reinit 8` after editing the profile.

- **Technical background:** <technical-background — default: non-developer / business founder, limited technical background>
- **Language:** <preferred-language — default: the language the founder writes in>
- **Explanation depth:** <explanation-depth — default: answer + brief reasoning; explain each technical term when it first appears>
- **Response length:** <response-length — default: short and to the point; avoid walls of text>
- **Domain expertise:** <domain — default: unknown; ask before assuming an analogy lands>

Calibrate language, length, and explanation depth to the above on every turn. When in doubt, apply the defaults: assume limited technical background, avoid unexplained jargon, offer a recommendation alongside open questions, and keep it short.

## Persistence convention

**Linear is canonical.** Every artifact produced in chat is written to a Linear document under the `[<MARKER>-DOC-NNNN]` pattern. The repo on GitHub is generated from Linear by Claude Code — chat-Claude never writes to local files.

Document type prefixes (allocated per `.claude/rules/counter-allocation.md` in the repo):

- `[<MARKER>-DOC-NNNN] discovery: state` — single mutable state document, updated each phase transition.
- `[<MARKER>-DOC-NNNN] discovery: idea-brief-v<N>` — one per iteration, append-only.
- `[<MARKER>-DOC-NNNN] discovery: challenge-memo-iter<N>` — one per iteration.
- `[<MARKER>-DOC-NNNN] research: <topic>` — one per research prompt; pairs with the deep report at `docs/research/NNNN-<slug>.md` (written by `/build` later).
- `[<MARKER>-DOC-NNNN] constitution: v<semver>` — seed and amendments.

## Skills location

Skills live in the repo under `.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`. Retrieve them via Project-knowledge search before invoking (they live in Project knowledge via the synced repo; there is no callable GitHub file-read tool). Active in chat:

- `/discovery` — five-phase north-star validation. Runs here.
- `/constitution` — drafts and amends `docs/constitution.md`. Runs here in seed mode; can also be invoked in Code for amendments.

Everything downstream (`/specify`, `/plan`, `/review`, `/build`, `/wrap`, `/verify`, `/retro`) runs in Claude Code, not chat.

## Where work happens

| Stage | Surface | Persistence target |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `/discovery` | chat | Linear doc |
| `/constitution` | chat | Linear doc + `docs/constitution.md` (Code writes the file) |
| `/specify` | code | Linear ticket + Linear doc + `docs/specs/NNNN-<slug>/spec.md` |
| `/plan`, `/review`, `/update-linear` | code | Linear ticket + Linear doc |
| `/build`, `/wrap` | code | Linear ticket + repo (git commits) |
| `/verify`, `/retro` | code | Linear doc + ticket |

## Rules (always-loaded — retrieve via Project-knowledge search)

- `.claude/rules/naming.md` — ticket IDs, slugs, file paths.
- `.claude/rules/counter-allocation.md` — how to allocate `NNNN` for new docs.
- `.claude/rules/scope-labels.md` — `scope:specified` / `scope:planned` / `scope:sealed` / `scope:built`.
- `.claude/rules/completion-status.md` — `DONE` / `DONE_WITH_CONCERNS` / `BLOCKED` / `NEEDS_CONTEXT`.
- `.claude/rules/write-discipline.md` — same-turn batching, no skill-chaining writes.
- `.claude/rules/auditor-stance.md` — voice and shape of critique output.

## Session discipline

- **One phase per chat turn.** `/discovery` is interactive — pause between Phases for founder confirmation.
- **Cite Linear doc IDs.** Every reference to prior state names the `[<MARKER>-DOC-NNNN]` it lives in. No "I remember from earlier in this chat" — chat memory is not durable.
- **Linear-first writes.** When in doubt, write to Linear, not the chat transcript.
- **Honor the Communication profile.** Read the Communication profile section above at the start of every chat and calibrate technical level, language, length, and explanation depth to it — don't re-ask what's already recorded.

## Notes

- **Do not put governing principles here.** Those live in `docs/constitution.md` (Code-authored). This file is chat-Claude's session instruction layer — equivalent to repo-side `CLAUDE.md`.
- **`<MARKER>` is substituted by `/onboard` step 8** at render time. Re-running `/onboard --reinit 8` regenerates this file.
